---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const emailPortfolio = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=AI%20Portfolio%20Builder%20%E2%80%94%20creator%20portfolio%20help";
const emailGeneral = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=AI%20Portfolio%20%E2%80%94%20general%20inquiry";
const calHref = "https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first";
---

<Layout
  title="AI Portfolio Builder: How AI Helps Creators Showcase Work | OKAD"
  description="Learn how AI portfolio builders help UGC creators present their work professionally. Tool comparison, best practices, and expert tips from an agency that manages 700+ creators."
>
  <Header />
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="pt-20 md:pt-24 pb-10 text-center bg-bg">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[12px] font-medium text-accent bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.18)] rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 mb-6">
          Open reference &middot; September 2026
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(28px,5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink mb-4">
          AI Portfolio Builder: <span class="text-accent">The Complete Guide</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-[18px] text-ink-2 max-w-[600px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-8">
          Brands spend under 90 seconds reviewing a creator portfolio. AI portfolio builders help you make every second count. This guide covers what they do, how they work, tool comparison, and the mistakes that cost creators brand deals.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap mb-8">
          <a href={emailPortfolio} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-accent text-white hover:bg-accent-hover transition-all no-underline">Get portfolio help &rarr;</a>
          <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-card text-ink border border-border hover:border-accent hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-5 flex-wrap justify-center font-mono text-[12px] text-muted">
          <span>700+ creators</span>
          <span>Setup &lt;10 min</span>
          <span>AI-powered</span>
          <span>Video native</span>
          <span>SEO indexed</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works grid -->
    <section class="py-8">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-center mb-5">What AI Portfolio Builders Do</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5">
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F50D;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Analyze Your Content</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">AI watches your videos, detects brands, identifies content types, and extracts metadata to power your portfolio.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x270D;&#xFE0F;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Generate Bio &amp; Descriptions</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">AI drafts your professional bio, project descriptions, and positioning statement. 80% usable out of the box.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F680;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Publish &amp; Share</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Get a shareable URL in minutes. Auto-updates when you add new work. Mobile-optimized and SEO-indexed.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TOC -->
    <section class="py-10 border-t border-b border-border">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-muted-2 mb-4">Contents</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-1.5">
          {[
            { num: "01", text: "Why Portfolios Matter", href: "#why-portfolios-matter" },
            { num: "02", text: "What AI Portfolio Builders Do", href: "#what-ai-portfolio-builders-do" },
            { num: "03", text: "How They Work Under the Hood", href: "#how-they-work" },
            { num: "04", text: "Tool Comparison", href: "#tool-comparison" },
            { num: "05", text: "Best Practices", href: "#best-practices" },
            { num: "06", text: "Common Mistakes", href: "#common-mistakes" },
            { num: "07", text: "SEO Tips", href: "#seo-tips" },
            { num: "08", text: "FAQ", href: "#faq" },
          ].map((item) => (
            <a href={item.href} class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[14px] text-ink-2 font-medium hover:bg-bg-alt transition-colors no-underline">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium text-accent min-w-[22px]">{item.num}</span>
              {item.text}
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 01 Why Portfolios Matter -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="why-portfolios-matter">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">01 &mdash; Why Portfolios Matter</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Why portfolios matter more than follower counts</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Brands hire based on work samples, not vanity metrics</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">A structured portfolio directly increases your booking rate</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Measured across hundreds of creator placements at OKAD</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The UGC industry has matured rapidly. Three years ago, a creator could land brand deals with a TikTok profile and a direct message. Today, brands receive dozens of pitches daily. What separates creators who book consistently from those who hear nothing back is almost always the same thing: a professional portfolio.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">At OKAD, we manage content production with a network of over 700 creators across beauty, tech, food, fitness, and lifestyle verticals. When a brand briefs us on a campaign, the first filter is never "who has the most followers." It is "who has relevant work I can review in under two minutes."</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A portfolio serves three critical functions. First, it proves you can actually produce the type of content the brand needs &mdash; not just similar content, but the exact format, tone, and production quality. Second, it demonstrates professionalism. A creator who invests time in presenting their work signals that they take deadlines, communication, and deliverables seriously. Third, it saves the brand manager time. When someone can review your best six videos on a single page without downloading anything, you have already won half the battle.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The problem is that building a portfolio has traditionally been tedious. Creators are not designers. They shoot video, not websites. This is exactly the gap that AI portfolio builders fill &mdash; and why every serious creator should understand how these tools work.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 What AI Portfolio Builders Do -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="what-ai-portfolio-builders-do">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">02 &mdash; What They Do</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">What AI portfolio builders actually do</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Automate writing descriptions, organizing content, detecting brands</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Generate a shareable page so you focus on creating, not designing</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Produce results equivalent to hours of manual work in under 10 minutes</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">An AI portfolio builder is any tool that uses machine learning to help creators assemble, organize, and present their work. The "AI" part handles tasks that would otherwise require either design skills or hours of manual effort.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Core capabilities most tools share</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Content analysis.</strong> AI watches your videos or scans your images and extracts key information &mdash; the brands featured, the type of content (testimonial, unboxing, tutorial), the hook structure, and sometimes even the emotional tone. This metadata powers everything else the tool does.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Bio and description generation.</strong> Based on the content you upload, AI drafts a professional bio, positioning statement, and individual project descriptions. The output is typically 80% usable out of the box &mdash; you tweak the tone and add personal details rather than staring at a blank page.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Layout and design automation.</strong> Instead of choosing fonts, spacing, and color palettes, the AI generates a visually coherent page layout. Most tools offer templates optimized for different content types &mdash; video-heavy portfolios get different layouts than photography or design portfolios.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Shareable output.</strong> The end product is a URL you can drop into emails, DMs, or your social media bio. No files to download, no access requests to approve. The brand manager clicks once and sees your work immediately.</li>
        </ol>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mt-6 mb-4">What makes these tools genuinely useful &mdash; not just novel &mdash; is the time savings. We have watched creators spend entire weekends building Canva decks that look decent but are painful to update. An AI portfolio builder produces something equivalent in under ten minutes. When you add a new project, the portfolio updates automatically. That alone changes the economics of maintaining a professional presence.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 How They Work -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="how-they-work">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">03 &mdash; Under the Hood</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">How AI portfolio builders work under the hood</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Upload content, AI processes it through vision and language models</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Five-step flow: upload, analyze, generate, review, publish</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Understanding the pipeline helps you get better results</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">While the exact technology varies by platform, most AI portfolio builders follow a similar pipeline. Understanding this process helps you get better results from whatever tool you choose.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The five-step pipeline</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Content ingestion.</strong> You upload videos, images, or links to published work. The tool stores your files and prepares them for analysis. For video content, this typically involves extracting keyframes, transcribing audio, and reading any on-screen text. For images, it means running object detection and text recognition.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>AI analysis.</strong> Vision models identify brands from logos, packaging, and product placement. Language models analyze transcripts to determine content type &mdash; is this a product review, a tutorial, an unboxing, or a lifestyle vignette? Some tools go deeper, identifying hook structures, call-to-action patterns, and even production quality markers like lighting consistency and audio clarity.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Content generation.</strong> Using everything learned from analysis, the AI generates your portfolio content. This includes your bio (tailored to the niches detected in your work), individual project descriptions, brand collaboration summaries, and sometimes even a "creative approach" section that describes your style based on patterns across your videos.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Layout assembly.</strong> The tool combines your content with a design template. Better tools are opinionated about layout &mdash; they place your strongest content first, group related work together, and ensure the page loads fast on mobile. The design should feel intentional without requiring you to make any design decisions.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Review and publish.</strong> You review the generated portfolio, make manual edits where needed, and publish. The output is a live URL. Good tools let you edit text freely without paying extra &mdash; AI credits should only apply to regenerating content, not to fixing a typo in your bio.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 Tool Comparison -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="tool-comparison">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">04 &mdash; Tool Comparison</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">AI portfolio tools compared</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Different tools suit different needs</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Dedicated UGC portfolio builders outperform general website builders</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Video-native tools understand creator content better</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Feature</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Google Drive / PDF</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Canva</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Linktree / Carrd</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">AI Portfolio Builder</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Setup time</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">2&ndash;4 hours</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">3&ndash;5 hours</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">30&ndash;60 min</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink font-semibold">Under 10 min</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">AI content writing</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">No</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Basic text AI</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">No</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink font-semibold">Full bio + descriptions</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Brand detection</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Manual</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Manual</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Manual</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink font-semibold">Automatic</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Video playback</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Download required</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Static images</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Embed only</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink font-semibold">Native player</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Auto-update</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Re-share needed</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Redesign needed</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Manual</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink font-semibold">Automatic</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Mobile optimized</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Often broken</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Limited</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Yes</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink font-semibold">Built for mobile</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">SEO discoverability</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Not indexed</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Not indexed</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Basic</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink font-semibold">Search indexed</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">Typical cost</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Free</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">$13/mo (Pro)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">$5&ndash;$24/mo</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink font-semibold">Free + optional credits</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Choosing the right tool for your situation</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">If you are a UGC creator whose work is primarily video, a dedicated AI portfolio builder will serve you far better than a general-purpose website builder. Generic tools treat video as an afterthought &mdash; you end up embedding YouTube links or uploading static thumbnails. Purpose-built tools offer native video playback, automatic content tagging, and layouts designed specifically for showcasing reels and short-form content.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">For creators who also do photography, graphic design, or illustration, a hybrid approach can work. Use an AI portfolio builder for your video work and a platform like Behance or Dribbble for static creative. Link between them so brands can see the full picture.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">We recommend avoiding the temptation to build a custom website with WordPress or Webflow unless you are also a web designer. The maintenance burden is real, and most creators abandon custom sites within three months because updating them requires technical effort they would rather spend creating.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Mid CTA -->
    <section class="py-10">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bg-dark rounded-2xl p-10 md:p-14 text-center">
          <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(22px,3.5vw,32px)] tracking-[-0.02em] text-white mb-3">Need help with your creator portfolio?</h2>
          <p class="text-[15px] text-muted max-w-[480px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-6">We work with 700+ UGC creators and help brands find the right talent. Whether you need portfolio strategy, content direction, or full creative production support, we can help.</p>
          <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap">
            <a href={emailPortfolio} class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-white text-ink hover:bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Get portfolio help &rarr;</a>
            <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold text-muted border border-white/15 hover:text-white hover:border-white/30 transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 Best Practices -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="best-practices">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">05 &mdash; Best Practices</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Best practices for AI-built portfolios</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Let AI do the heavy lifting, but always review and personalize</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Lead with your strongest work, keep descriptions concise</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Make your contact information impossible to miss</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">1. Curate ruthlessly before uploading</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">AI will analyze whatever you feed it. If you upload twenty mediocre videos, your portfolio will look mediocre no matter how good the AI is at writing descriptions. Select your five to eight strongest pieces. Prioritize variety &mdash; different brands, different content types, different tones. A brand manager wants to see range, not repetition.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">2. Edit the AI-generated text</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">AI-written bios are a solid starting point, but they tend to be generic. Add specific details that only you know &mdash; your turnaround time, your preferred content formats, the industries you understand deeply. Replace vague phrases like "passionate about creating engaging content" with concrete facts like "specialize in 15&ndash;30 second testimonial-style ads for DTC skincare brands."</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">3. Put your best reel first</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The first video in your portfolio gets 4&ndash;5x more plays than the last one. This is not a guess &mdash; we have tracked this across creator profiles for two years. Lead with the piece that best represents the work you want to do more of. If you want beauty brand deals, lead with your best beauty reel, even if your food content has more views.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">4. Include rates or a rate range</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">This is controversial, but our data is clear: creators who include at least a rate range ("$200&ndash;500 per video depending on complexity") receive more qualified inquiries than those who say "DM for rates." Brands have budgets. When they can see your range fits their budget, they reach out. When it is hidden, they often move to the next creator who makes it easy.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">5. Make contact information prominent</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">This sounds obvious, but we regularly see portfolios where the only way to contact the creator is to scroll to the bottom and find a small email link. Your email address and preferred contact method should be visible without scrolling. Include it near the top and again at the bottom. Remove any friction between "I want to work with this person" and "I just sent them a message."</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">6. Test on mobile before sharing</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Over 60% of portfolio views happen on phones. Brand managers check creator portfolios between meetings, during commutes, and while reviewing pitch emails on their phones. Open your portfolio on your own phone before you send it anywhere. Check that videos play without issues, text is readable, and your CTA buttons are tappable.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

