    <!-- 07 SEO Tips -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="seo-tips">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">07 &mdash; SEO Tips</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">SEO tips to make your portfolio discoverable</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">A discoverable portfolio brings inbound leads without cold pitching</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Optimize page title, use niche-specific keywords naturally</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Make sure your portfolio is indexable by search engines</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Most creators think of their portfolio as something they send out in pitches. But a well-optimized portfolio also works as an inbound channel &mdash; brands searching for "UGC creator beauty Portugal" or "tech product video creator English" can find you without you ever reaching out.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Use a descriptive page title</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Your portfolio page title should include your name, your primary niche, and the word "UGC" or "creator." A good example: "Sarah Chen &mdash; Beauty UGC Creator Portfolio." Avoid generic titles like "My Work" or "Portfolio" &mdash; they tell search engines nothing useful.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Write natural, keyword-rich descriptions</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">When you edit your AI-generated bio, include the specific terms brands search for. Mention content types (testimonial ads, product demos, unboxing videos), platforms (TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts), and industries (skincare, SaaS, food and beverage). Do not stuff keywords &mdash; write for humans first, search engines second.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Ensure your portfolio is indexable</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Not all portfolio tools are created equal here. Some generate client-side-rendered pages that search engines cannot crawl effectively. Check if your portfolio appears in Google by searching "site:yourtool.com/your-name" after it has been live for a week. If it does not show up, your tool may not support proper SEO &mdash; consider switching to one that does.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Add alt text to images and video thumbnails</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">If your portfolio tool allows custom alt text, use it. Describe what is in each video thumbnail &mdash; "UGC testimonial ad for organic skincare brand" is far more useful than "video-1.jpg." This helps with image search visibility and accessibility, both of which matter.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Link to your portfolio from other platforms</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Add your portfolio URL to your Instagram bio, TikTok bio, LinkedIn profile, Twitter/X bio, and email signature. Each link signals to search engines that this page matters. More importantly, it creates multiple entry points for brands to discover your work regardless of where they first encounter you.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

